STRDUP(3)                      P32W Unix                       STRDUP(3)

NAME
       strdup - copy a string into new memory

SYNOPSIS
       #include <string.h>

       char *strdup(const char *s);

DESCRIPTION
       strdup copies the string s, NUL included, into memory from
       malloc(3) and returns the copy. free(3) releases it.

RETURN VALUE
       The copy, or NULL if there is not enough memory.

EXAMPLES
       names[n++] = strdup(e->d_name);

SEE ALSO
       string(3), malloc(3)

BUGS
       There is no strndup.
